> Mouse protein coding genes were extracted from https://www.ensembl.org/biomart on 15.05.2018 using the following filters:

Ensembl Genes 92

Mouse genes: GRCm38.p6
Attributes: MGI symbol
Gene type: protein_coding

mt- and MT- were removed manually from mitochondrial gene IDs.

> Expression data from:

An RNA-Seq atlas of gene expression in mouse and rat normal tissues



> GO Slim is the generic GO Slim from:

http://www.geneontology.org/page/go-subset-guide

Then the OBO file was read into R with:

mgi <- get_ontology("data/goslim_generic.obo",
                    propagate_relationships =
                      get_relation_names("data/goslim_generic.obo"),
                    extract_tags = "everything")

> GO annotations per Gene from the MGI:

http://www.informatics.jax.org/gotools/data/input/MGIgenes_by_GOid.txt


> MeSH tree numbers from:
	ftp://nlmpubs.nlm.nih.gov/online/mesh/MESH_FILES/meshtrees/

> Associations of human and mouse genes with Disease Ontology (DO) diseases
	http://www.informatics.jax.org/humanDisease.shtml
	http://www.informatics.jax.org/downloads/reports/MGI_DO.rpt








LEGACY...
Downloaded file http://www.informatics.jax.org/gotools/data/input/mgi_go_slim.go
and parsed it into the OBO ontology format with perl package GO::Parser:

sudo apt install libgo-perl
go2fmt -w obo_text mgi_go_slim.go > mgi_go_slim.obo

